  "id": "selective-permeability",
  "term": "selective permeability",
  "definition": "Selective permeability is the property of a cell barrier that allows some substances to pass through while limiting others. In the packet, it refers to tight junctions between epithelial cells regulating the movement of ions, small molecules, and larger substances so unwanted materials are kept out.",
